{
  "name": "Echo",
  "created": "2026-09-13T18:00:00.000Z",
  "notes": "Every kick throws a comet outward from the centre, and the room throws it back twice: once after Echo Gap, and again after twice that, each fainter and a shade further toward violet.\n\nThe echoes are `delay` nodes. `M2` delays the kick's edge, and `M3` delays `M2`'s, so one Gap knob spaces both and the second echo always lands at twice the first. A delay keeps a queue, so a kick arriving while an echo is still on its way adds another rather than cancelling it.\n\nEach delay also CARRIES a value: `M2` reads the bass band on the frame the kick arrives and publishes that reading on the frame its echo leaves, and `M3` carries `M2`'s on again. That value sets the echo's launch speed, so a hard kick's echoes fly as far as the kick did -- without the carry, an echo would launch at whatever the music happened to be doing a third of a second later.",
